---
// Two doors, restructured (preview variant). Same door headings and
// overall framing as the live section; door bodies replaced with the
// tighter locked copy, each linking out to the full essay.
---

<section id="doors" class="doors-section" aria-labelledby="doors-heading">
  <div class="doors-inner">
    <header class="doors-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Two doors</p>
      <h2 id="doors-heading" class="doors-headline">
        Run your organization. Extend yourself.
      </h2>
      <p class="doors-sub">
        Minsky is useful in two different shapes. Neither is the main one — pick whichever
        matches what you are trying to do.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="doors-grid">
      <article class="door">
        <h3 class="door-title">Run your organization</h3>
        <p class="door-body">
          Software work holds together because of the structure around the coding: tracked
          work, isolated changes, independent review, recorded decisions. Minsky builds that
          structure into the environment — each task in its own workspace, every merge gated
          on adversarial review, standards enforced by hooks that bind humans and agents
          identically. You state what should happen; the environment carries it to reviewed,
          merged work.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/structure-gap">Read the full argument →</a>
      </article>

      <article class="door">
        <h3 class="door-title">Extend yourself</h3>
        <p class="door-body">
          Run serious work through agents and the whole picture ends up in your head — eight
          sessions, five projects, chats everywhere. Minsky keeps that picture outside your
          skull: the cockpit shows everything in flight and surfaces what needs you; questions
          land in one inbox with the context to decide; what the system learns, it keeps. The
          place you inspect your work becomes the place work starts.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/structure-gap">Read the full argument →</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .doors-section {
    padding: 5rem 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in oklch, var(--color-text-primary) 4%, transparent);
  }
  .doors-inner {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3rem;
  }
  .doors-header {
    max-width: 640px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }
  .doors-headline {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: clamp(1.875rem, 3.8vw, 2.75rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .doors-sub {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .doors-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 2.5rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 860px) {
    .doors-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 3rem;
    }
  }

  .door {
    padding: 2rem;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in oklch, var(--color-text-primary) 8%, transparent);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background-color: var(--color-bg-elevated);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.125rem;
  }
  .door-title {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .door-body {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .text-link {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--color-signal);
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    transition: color 160ms ease;
    align-self: flex-start;
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
  }
  .text-link:hover {
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }
</style>
